---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Privacy Policy"
	description="How Revenue Driven Marketing collects, uses, and protects information across this website and our Meta Marketing API integration."
>
	<article class="policy">
		<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
		<p class="updated">Last updated: August 4, 2026</p>

		<p>
			This policy explains how Revenue Driven Marketing ("we," "us") handles information
			collected through this website (revenuedrivenmarketing.com) and through our use of the
			Meta Marketing API to manage advertising accounts for our agency and our authorized
			clients.
		</p>

		<h2>Information We Collect</h2>

		<h3>Information You Provide</h3>
		<p>
			When you submit our contact form, we collect your name, email address, and any details you
			include in your message (such as current ad spend). This is processed through Formspree, a
			third-party form service, and used solely to respond to your inquiry.
		</p>

		<h3>Information Collected Automatically</h3>
		<p>
			We use Google Analytics (GA4) and Google Tag Manager to understand how visitors use this
			site &mdash; pages viewed, general usage patterns, and referral sources. This data is
			aggregated and does not include sensitive personal information.
		</p>

		<h3>Meta Advertising Data</h3>
		<p>
			We operate a Meta Marketing API integration, authorized through Meta Business Manager via a
			System User token, to create, manage, and report on advertising campaigns for ad accounts
			and Pages that we or our authorized clients control. This integration accesses ad account,
			Page, campaign, and creative data &mdash; it does not collect personal data from individual
			consumers who view or interact with the ads themselves.
		</p>

		<h2>How We Use Information</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>To respond to inquiries submitted through this site.</li>
			<li>To create, manage, optimize, and report on advertising campaigns on behalf of our agency and our authorized clients.</li>
			<li>To understand and improve how this website performs.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>Meta Platform Data</h2>
		<p>
			Our use of the Meta Marketing API is limited to providing advertising management services
			for accounts we or our clients have granted us access to through Business Manager. We do
			not use Meta Platform Data for any purpose beyond delivering those services, and we do not
			sell Meta Platform Data to any third party. Access can be revoked at any time by removing
			our System User's permissions in Business Manager.
		</p>

		<h2>Cookies &amp; Analytics</h2>
		<p>
			This site uses cookies and similar technologies via Google Analytics and Google Tag
			Manager. You can opt out of Google Analytics tracking using the
			<a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
				Google Analytics Opt-out Browser Add-on
			</a>, or block cookies entirely through your browser settings.
		</p>

		<h2>Third-Party Service Providers</h2>
		<p>We rely on the following services to operate this site and our advertising management work:</p>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Meta</strong> &mdash; advertising account and campaign management via the Marketing API.</li>
			<li><strong>Google Analytics &amp; Google Tag Manager</strong> &mdash; site analytics and tag management.</li>
			<li><strong>Formspree</strong> &mdash; contact form processing.</li>
			<li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> &mdash; website hosting and content delivery.</li>
			<li><strong>GitHub</strong> &mdash; source code and content version control.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>Each provider has its own privacy practices governing the data it processes on our behalf.</p>

		<h2>Data Sharing</h2>
		<p>
			We do not sell personal information. We share information only with the service providers
			listed above, as necessary to operate this site and deliver our advertising management
			services, or when required by law.
		</p>

		<h2>Data Retention</h2>
		<p>
			Contact form submissions and analytics data are retained only as long as necessary to
			respond to inquiries and understand site performance. Meta advertising data is retained
			only as long as we are actively managing the associated ad accounts.
		</p>

		<h2>Your Rights</h2>
		<p>
			Depending on your location, you may have the right to access, correct, or request deletion
			of personal information we hold about you. To exercise any of these rights, contact us at
			the email below.
		</p>

		<h2>Data Deletion</h2>
		<p>
			To request deletion of personal information you've submitted to us (for example, through
			our contact form), email us at
			<a href="mailto:marketingbykareem@gmail.com">marketingbykareem@gmail.com</a> and we will
			delete it within a reasonable timeframe. Access to Meta advertising data is controlled
			directly through Business Manager &mdash; removing our System User's permissions there
			immediately revokes our access to that account's data.
		</p>

		<h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
		<p>
			This site and our services are not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly
			collect personal information from children.
		</p>

		<h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
		<p>
			We may update this policy from time to time. Changes will be posted on this page with an
			updated "Last updated" date.
		</p>

		<h2>Contact Us</h2>
		<p>
			Questions about this policy? Email us at
			<a href="mailto:marketingbykareem@gmail.com">marketingbykareem@gmail.com</a>.
		</p>
	</article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.policy {
		max-width: 68ch;
	}
	h1 {
		font-size: 2rem;
		margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
	}
	.updated {
		color: var(--color-text-muted);
		font-size: 0.9rem;
		margin-top: 0;
	}
	h2 {
		font-size: 1.3rem;
		margin-top: 2.25rem;
	}
	h3 {
		font-size: 1.05rem;
		margin-top: 1.5rem;
	}
	ul {
		padding-left: 1.25rem;
	}
	li {
		margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
	}
</style>
